\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 2-Polish bonds surge,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  plays down Ukraine impact\b0\par\par\uc2 1,021 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 18:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Polish 10-year yield at 4-month low after cbank cuts CPI\par forecast\par     * Forint firms as data shows pick-up in Hungary growth\par     * Leu surges as Romanian president ends IMF deal stand-off\par     * Richter shares fall, reminder of risks over Ukraine\par \par     By Sandor Peto\par     BUDAPEST, March 5 (Reuters) - Polish government bonds surged\par on Wednesday after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its inflation\par forecast and said the zloty could weather any turbulence caused\par by the crisis in Ukraine.\par     Other Central European assets firmed for a second straight\par day, helped by data confirming economic growth in the region as\par local factors overshadowed events in neighbouring Ukraine for\par the first time in over two weeks.\par     Poland's 10-year bond yield, which moves\par inversely to prices, fell 17 basis points to 4.18 percent, its\par lowest level in four months. The zloty was flat.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept rates on hold as expected and\par extended its guidance for keeping its key interest rate at a\par record low 2.5 percent at least until September, instead of\par June.\par     The bank cut inflation forecasts for this year and its\par governor Marek Belka said the zloty could resist\par contagion effects from neighbouring Ukraine where the crisis\par would have a marginal impact on Poland's economic growth.\par     "The inflation projection is very positive, there's no\par pressure whatsoever, reaching the inflation target is only\par planned in 2016. This shows that there's a good period for bonds\par ahead of us," said Pekao SA analyst Arkadiusz Urbanski.\par     Elsewhere, the leu surged half a percent versus\par the euro after Romania's president signed the review of an IMF\par aid agreement seen as key to Romania's economic credibility.\par  \par     The Hungarian forint firmed 0.3 percent.\par     Hungarian bonds extended Tuesday's gains posted after\par Russian President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vladimir Putin\f28 \uc2 \f2  said he saw no need for now to\par use military force in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ukraine\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after Russia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par Crimea region.\par     Analysts said spillover effects from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ukraine\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and other\par volatile emerging markets remained a risk. A Reuters poll,\par however, forecast that the region's economic recovery could help\par the forint and the zloty firm 3.5 percent against the euro in\par the next 12 months. \par     Shares of Hungarian drug maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gedeon Richter\f28 \uc2 \f2 ,\par which has significant sales in both Ukraine and Russia, plunged\par 6 percent in a reminder of contagion risks from the crisis.\par     Richter's Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Erik Bogsch\f28 \uc2 \f2  warned that the firm\par expected its first-quarter operating profit margin to plumb\par record lows due to the fall in the value of the Russian rouble,\par as Russia is the company's biggest market.      \par     \par     MORE SWINGS POSSIBLE\par     Further market jitters are still possible as contagion risks\par from other emerging economies linger, some traders warned.\par     "Most market players look more optimistic than me at the\par moment," one Budapest-based fixed income trader said.\par     "I will be right in the end, but that is thin comfort if\par before that I have to close my positions," he said.\par     Hungarian assets have been particularly vulnerable despite\par the country's big trade surplus. It is the most indebted state\par in the region and some investors also fret that it may have cut\par interest rates too low given the contagion risks.\par     Investors have been withdrawing capital from emerging\par economies for months as a cutback in U.S. monetary stimulus has\par triggered risk aversion.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has cut its base rate to 2.7 percent\par from a peak of 7 percent in 2012. Its last cut in February\par defied wobbles in emerging markets, and even though the bank\par indicated caution, it did not rule out further monetary easing.\par     The forint hit a two-year low against the euro last month.\par On Monday, the bank's deputy governor Adam Balog called the\par forint's recent moves a "smaller turbulence", caused by global\par factors rather than the rate cuts. \par     "The market understands, feels and has priced in that the\par current forint levels are fine to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and that\par they will not try to calm down markets, only if the forint falls\par beyond 320," one Budapest-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealer said.\par     "I can easily imagine now that they will continue to cut\par rates," the dealer said.\par     The forint was bid at 309.50 at 1639 GMT.\par                       CEE MARKETS SNAPSHOT AT 1739 CET\par  ************************** \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ************************\par                              Latest  Previous   Daily   Change\par                              bid     close      change  in 2014\par  Czech crown                 27.339    27.355  +0.06%  -0.03%\par  Hungarian forint           309.500   310.440  +0.30%  -4.05%\par  Polish zloty                 4.188     4.188    0.00%  -0.92%\par  Romanian leu                 4