\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro rises versus yen as geopolitical risk fears ebb\b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 09:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Russian news agencies say Putin orders troops in military exercise back to base\par \par \uc2 * Euro edges higher on the reports, yen extends earlier losses\par \par \uc2 * No news on movement of Russian forces in Crimea (Repeats to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 By Masayuki Kitano\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, March 4 (Reuters) - The euro rose against the yen on Tuesday following reports that Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has ordered troops who took part in military exercises in central and western Russia to return to base.\par \par \uc2 The euro rose to intraday highs versus both the yen and the dollar after the reports by Russian news agencies, which quoted the Kremlin spokesman.\par \par \uc2 Moscow had denied that the exercises, which began last week and ended on schedule, had anything to do with events in Ukraine, where Putin has said he has the right to deploy troops to protect Russian compatriots. There was no news of Russian troop movements in Crimea.\par \par \uc2 The euro rose 0.1 percent to $1.3752, after rising to about $1.3767 at one point. Against the yen, the euro gained 0.4 percent to 139.96 yen, having risen to as high as 140.35 yen at one point.\par \par \uc2 The safe-haven yen slipped broadly, helping the dollar rise 0.3 percent to 101.75 yen. The greenback pulled away from a one-month low of 101.20 yen that had been set on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "There is some unwinding of long positions in the yen and long positions in the Swiss franc, but it's hard to tell at this point if the trend has changed," said Satoshi Okagawa, senior global markets analyst for \uc2 Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corporation\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Risk sentiment has been hit of late by the crisis over Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 , boosting safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the yen and the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's forces have tightened their grip on the Russian-speaking Crimea region, a move described by U.S. President Barack Obama as a violation of international law and of Ukraine's sovereignty.\par \par \uc2 The dollar could extend its recent fall against the yen if risk sentiment worsens further, although the yen's gains could be limited by speculation that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  might eventually step up its monetary stimulus, said Sim Moh Siong, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Bank of Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "I think in the back of the market's mind...is always the backstop, in terms of BOJ," Sim said.\par \par \uc2 Many market participants expect the BOJ to take further easing steps at some point to achieve its 2 percent inflation target, although expectations for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act soon have faded recently as BOJ Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  remains doggedly positive that the economy is improving.\par \par \uc2 "If the Ukraine situation escalates, and that leads to a global risk-off, and perhaps higher oil prices as well...Japanese policymakers would have to reassess the economic impact on Japan and that may prompt a policy response," he added.\par \par \uc2 The Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Crimean peninsula has rattled oil markets, with U.S. crude rising to its highest settlement price in 5-1/2 months on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Trading in the Australian dollar was somewhat choppy after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  kept interest rates steady at a record low of 2.50 percent, as widely expected, and reiterated that the most prudent course for policy was likely a period of stability.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie dollar rose to around $0.8970 or so right after the RBA decision, but later faltered when the RBA said in its post-meeting statement that the Australian dollar's exchange rate remains high by historical standards.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar was last steady on the day at $0.8936 , staying above a one-month low of $0.8891 that had been set on Monday. (Additional reporting by Ian Chua in Sydney) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-4T09:36:26.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140304ea3400bnh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
