\par\par \b \uc2 Russia Halts Buying of Foreign  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Due to Market Volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh \par \uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 10:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--\uc2 Russia's finance ministry\uc2  said Tuesday it had halted the buying of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the reserve fund due to increased financial market volatility, which should ease downside pressure on the ruble.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry started buying 3.5 billion rubles ($95.9 million) of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the open market on Feb. 20 to stash the extra revenues from oil and gas exports in the rainy-day reserve fund.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry's decision to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth 212.2 billion rubles by the end of May had a negative impact on the ruble in February despite the ministry's claim that its purchases won't have an impact on the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the ruble plummeted to its new lows against the dollar and the euro due to heavy selloff triggered by threats of sanctions from the West in response to Moscow's decision to send troops to \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to change its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mechanism to stop the ruble from falling and sold more than $10.5 billion from its gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's fourth largest. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also unexpectedly raised interest rates by 1.5 percentage points to ease downside pressure on the ruble.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry said it has bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth 38 billion rubles for the reserve fund so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 04, 2014 04:17 ET (09:17 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140304ea340010j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
