\f2 Baader Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects \f28 \uc2 \f2 Beiersdorf\f28 \uc2 \f2 's guidance to be rather cautious given the ongoing slump in the personal care environment in developed regions and adverse exchange rate movements in emerging markets. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bankhaus Lampe\f28 \uc2 \f2  also notes "a possible turnaround in China boosting outlook for 2014." \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RWE AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  (RWE.XE): 2013 Earnings \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Due: March 4 at 0600 GMT\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Survey of 9 Analysts\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Average Recurrent After-Tax Profit: EUR 2.41B, down 2% (EUR 2.46B in 2012)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Average Operating Profit: EUR 5.93B, down 7.6% (EUR 6.42B in 2012)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Average Revenue: EUR 53.92B, up 1.3% (EUR 53.23B in 2012)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Note: RWE's earnings is seen falling due to the erosion of wholesale power prices by subsidized renewable energies that are squeezing large power plants out of the market. Last month, RWE announced renewed write-downs on power plants of EUR 3.3 billion, saying this will result in the company's first annual net loss. A Dow Jones Newswires calculation shows that the 2013 net loss will amount to nearly EUR 3 billion. Focus will be on 2014 guidance, which some analysts said could be questioned due to warm weather, and more pressure on power prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 4 Mar 2014 00:00 EDT \par European Morning Briefing: Other Scheduled Events\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * denotes events waiting for confirmation\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Abcam (ABC.LN) Interim 2014 Results\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Abcam (ABC.LN) Interim 2014 Analyst meeting\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aegean Airlines\f28 \uc2 \f2  (AEGN.AT) Full year 2013 Results\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Arbonia Forster Holding AG (AFGN.EB) Full year 2013 Press & analyst meeting\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Arbonia Forster Holding AG (AFGN.EB) Full year 2013 Results\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Arkema\f28 \uc2 \f2  (AKE.FR) Full year 2013 