\uc2 \f2 Ringkjobing Landbobank\f28 \uc2 \f2  (RILBA.KO) Full year 2013 Dividend payment date - proposed (seen 15.00000)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ringkjobing Landbobank\f28 \uc2 \f2  (RILBA.KO) Special dividend payment date - proposed (seen 10.00000)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Royal Caribbean Cruises\f28 \uc2 \f2  (RCL) Q1 2014 Dividend payment date (seen 0.25000)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 04, 2014 00:00 ET (05:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140304ea34000m9\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: Dollar rises as investors seek for safe-haven\b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par \uc2 News Bites - Private Companies\par \uc2 NBPRCO\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014. News Bites Pty Ltd.   \par \par \uc2 NEWS BITES - PRIVATE COMPANIES\par \par \uc2 [Company Release]\par \par \uc2 U.S. Dollar advanced on Monday trading session together with the Japanese Yen as investors seek for safe-haven assets after the Russian Federation entered Ukraine's Crimea peninsula raising political tension in the country. The so-called Greenback increased pushing the Dollar index 0.3% higher to 79.885, while the Yen added as much as 0.6% against the Euro to 139.67.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41101/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS NEWS ROUND UP\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Hryvnia falls to record low as Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Hryvnia declined on Monday trading session falling towards the lowest level all-time after the Russian Federation \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  into \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Crimea peninsula raising concerns over possible war conflict as the Russian President Putin declares his troops had right to enter the country.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41103/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: U.S. personal spending and income both advance in January\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] Personal spending and income in the U.S. increased in January at a notable faster pace than experts originally estimated, a report published by the Commerce Department showed on Monday. According to the report, the U.S. personal income gained 0.3% in January compared to a 0.2% jump estimated earlier, while personal spending climbed 0.4% in the same month. Source: Company Website\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41108/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: Bank of Russia raises rates by 150 basis points\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russian increased its benchmark interest rates unexpectedly on Monday amid raising concerns over possible war conflict in neighboring Ukraine pushing the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Ruble towards the historical low versus the U.S. Dollar. The Bank of Russia raised the rate by 150 basis points from 5.50% to 7.00%. Source: Company Website\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41104/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: U.S. construction spending rises slower in January\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] Construction spending in the world's largest economy surprisingly eased at the beginning of 2014, however it stayed in positive territory suggesting that the sector is growing, a report released by the Commerce Department showed on Monday. The U.S. construction spending advanced 0.1% rising from December's level of $941.9 billion to a level of $943.1 billion recorded in January. Source: Company Website\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41107/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: Portugal industrial output rises slower in January\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] Industrial production in Portugal advanced at the beginning of 2014, however the pace of growth was lower than economists preliminary estimated, a data published by the statistical office unveiled on Monday. The country's industrial output gained 3.9% on an annual basis in January after rising by 5.7% in the last month of 2013. Source: Company Website\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41106/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 Dokument NBPRCO0020140304ea34001xq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
