\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen holds ground as Ukraine jitters keep risk at bay\b0\par\par\uc2 547 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 00:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yen among best performing major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight\par \par \uc2 * Concerns about Ukraine still dampening risk appetite\par \par \uc2 * RBA rate review to offer some distraction for Aussie dollar\par \par \uc2 By Ian Chua\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY, March 4 (Reuters) - The yen held onto chunky gains early on Tuesday, having been squeezed higher as skittish investors dumped riskier assets amid tensions over Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The euro traded at 139.30 yen after falling 0.8 percent on Monday, while the dollar fetched 101.43 yen not far from a one-month low of 101.20.\par \par \uc2 Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's forces have tightened their grip on the Russian-speaking Crimea region, a move described by U.S. President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  as a violation of international law and of Ukraine's sovereignty.\par \par \uc2 Obama warned his government would look at a series of economic and diplomatic sanctions that would isolate Russia, which on Monday saw its stocks, bonds and rouble plummet.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked its key lending rates and spent as much as $12 billion of its reserves in a desperate attempt to prop up the rouble.\par \par \uc2 Heightened geopolitical tensions took their toll on global stocks but traditional safe havens including gold, U.S. Treasuries and German Bunds all rallied.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the yen was the main beneficiary. The U.S. dollar was also in favour, further helped by a batch of encouraging U.S. economic data.\par \par \uc2 U.S. factory activity rebounded from an eight-month low last month and consumer spending increased more than expected in January, suggesting the economy was regaining some strength after abruptly slowing in recent months.\par \par \uc2 "The overall tone of the data is optimistic with the major sentiment surveys surprising to the upside. Hence this should alleviate some of the weather-related concerns and be USD-supportive," \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  analysts wrote in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 The euro last stood at $1.3735, having fallen 0.5 percent on Monday. This helped the dollar index climb to 80.063, pulling away from a two-month trough of 79.688 plumbed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc, usually seen as a safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , lost a bit of steam after scaling a two-year peak against the dollar and a one-year high on the euro.\par \par \uc2 Commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which tend to be sold off in times of heightened market stress, showed remarkable resilience. The Australian dollar, for example, edged up to $0.8935 having hit a one-month trough $0.8891.\par \par \uc2 The focus for Aussie punters is the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2 's (RBA) policy review due out at 0330 GMT.\par \par \uc2 The RBA, however, is almost certain to keep the cash rate at a record low 2.5 percent, having already said last month that it saw a period of stability in policy.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been surprisingly resilient despite heavy anti-risk sentiment at the start of the week, which may reflect investors' unwillingness to take directional bets until the RBA announcement is behind them," said Ilya Spivak, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at DailyFX.\par \par \uc2 "Once event risk passes, pent-up selling pressure may be released and send the Aussie below support near the 0.89 level to the U.S. dollar." \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-4T00:12:34.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140303ea3300zhv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
