\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's hryvnia sinks again;  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  stymied by dwindling foreign reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalia Zinets   \par \uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2014\par 11:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Feb 27 (Reuters) - Ukraine's hryvnia fell to a new record low against the dollar on Thursday as investors kept far away from a country in turmoil with a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stymied by dwindling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 The political situation in Ukraine remained tense. Armed men seized the regional government headquarters and parliament in Crimea on Thursday and raised the Russian flag.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 11.0 to the dollar on the Reuters dealing platform, and forward markets were pricing it to trade weaker at 11.65 per dollar in six months' time.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's dollar bond maturing in June 2014 fell slightly to 93.94 cents to the dollar, although other dollar bonds ticked higher on the prospect of Western financial aid.\par \par \uc2 The hryvnia has been falling for weeks but has accelerated since parliament stripped President Viktor Yanukovich of his powers on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 "If we look at historical precedents, five years ago the hryvnia was much stronger versus the U..S dollar. The economy was in a better shape, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were almost double current levels but the hryvnia depreciated almost 50 percent," said Tatyana Orlova, a strategist at RBS in London.\par \par \uc2 "If you take that as the benchmark it could go to 16 per dollar," she said.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's interim leaders have said they will put the country back on course for European integration and a new government is expected to be sworn in on Thursday. A presidential election is due on May 25.\par \par \uc2 Kiev has also asked the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  to help prepare a new financial aid programme as it tries to meet its debt payments and an anti-crisis plan is being drawn up.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not plan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming days, the bank's governor, Stepan Kubiv, said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, a senior official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had said it had abandoned a managed exchange rate policy in favour of a flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ..\par \par \uc2 Orlova said the hyrvnia could easily "overshoot" if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but added: "A big devaluation is not unjustified for the economy."\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-2T10:42:32.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140227ea2r007hq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
