\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso dips on Fed minutes, Ukraine bonds dive\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michael O'Boyle and Christine Murray   \par \uc2 842 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2014\par 22:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Feb 19 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Wednesday after minutes from the last U.S. Federal Reserve meeting suggested policymakers would keep up the pace of a withdrawal of monetary stimulus.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Ukraine's bond prices fell as more violence hit Kiev, while mounting unrest in Venezuela drove the price of its credit default swaps to near five-year highs.\par \par \uc2 Emerging market assets have slumped since last May on expectations that less monetary stimulus will drive up U.S. yields and pull back a tide of investment that had flooded into emerging markets in recent years.\par \par \uc2 Minutes of the Fed's Jan. 28-29 policy meeting, released on Wednesday, showed several officials wanted to drive home the idea that their asset-purchase program would be trimmed in predictable, $10-billion steps unless there is a big economic surprise this year.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso and the South African rand, two of the most liquid emerging market assets, slipped to their weakest levels in nearly one week after the Fed minutes.\par \par \uc2 Many emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had steadied in February after sharp drops in January, but views on the Fed could drive more selling, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "I think we are back to selling emerging markets," said Win Thin, an analyst at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York. "The tapering is unfolding and at some point we have to talk about rate hikes. That is the next shoe to drop."\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso posted its bigest decline against the dollar in more than two weeks, the day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates by 25 basis points and maintained its bias towards more easing as the top copper exporter's economy runs out of steam.\par \par \uc2 Turkey and Brazil have been raising interest rates to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fight the risk that higher import prices could drive up inflation.\par \par \uc2 Analysts note that easy money policies from the Fed had driven gains in emerigng market assets across the board as investors sought out higher yields.\par \par \uc2 But the witdrawal of that global liquidity is now exposing emerging markets with political and economic problems.\par \par \uc2 Worries about Argentina and Turkey sparked indiscriminate selling of emerging market assets in January but analysts said problems in the Ukraine and Venezuela would not spark a similar global selloff. Some even see signs of a bottom.\par \par \uc2 "We think that this is a temporary situation that will not last," veteran investor \uc2 Mark Mobius\uc2 , chairman of \uc2 Templeton Emerging Markets\uc2  Group, said at a conference in Mexico City. "We're nearing the bottom of this exodus."\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, VENEZUELA PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 Protesters poured into a central Kiev square on Wednesday, a day after at least 25 people were killed in demonstrations. Protests that began in November have hit the Ukraine's heavily indebted economy and drained the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 Russia is a key supporter of Ukraine's government, but has so far agreed to pay only $2 billion of a promised $15 billion aid package. Protestors are demanding Ukraine embrace a wide-reaching trade deal with the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , over Russia's objections.\par \par \uc2 Prices for Ukraine's dollar bonds fell, with the 2020 dollar bond down 0.41 cents of a dollar while the bond maturing in 2023 hit an all-time low. The hryvnia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a fresh five-year low.\par \par \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  said Ukraine could face a liquidity crunch in the next few months, noting the country has mounting debt payments while foreign reserves are at an eight-year low after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent about 8 percent of its reserves on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January alone.\par \par \uc2 While mounting violence in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  is troubling on many levels, Mobius said worries that it could wreck the economy are overblown.\par \par \uc2 "Despite all the bad news that you hear about Ukraine actually they're in a very sweet spot" economically, Mobius said, noting that "they have the Europeans who want to help them and they have the Russians who want to help them."\par \par \uc2 Neighboring Russia saw its rouble hit an all-time low versus the euro after the finance ministry said it plans to buy nearly $6 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to replenish one of its sovereign wealth funds.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark MSCI equity index dipped 0.19 percent with strong Chinese stocks countering negative sentiment from Ukraine and Russia.\par \par \uc2 Student-led protests in Venezuela over issues including inflation, crime, corruption and product shortages continued to flare after security forces arrested opposition leader Leopoldo Lopez on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Investors reacted by driving up the cost of insuring Venezuela's debt for five years to its highest since April 2009 .\par \par \uc2 Debt prices have fallen to levels often associated with a nation at or near default. Still, Venezuela's vast oil reserves have lent support, giving investors comfort they will be repaid.\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see )\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-2-22T21:33:54.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140219ea2j00gwe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
