\par\par \b \uc2 Ukraine's  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  reserves fall to $17.8 bln due to debt repayments,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  - cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 137 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2014\par 13:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Feb 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $17.805 billion as of Jan 31 - their lowest level since 2006 - compared with $20.416 billion at the end of December, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The bank, in a statement, attributed the drop to total debt repayments of $1.1 billion, including $650 million to the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , as well as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  totalling $1.7 billion on the interbank market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past 10 days has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to help the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the hryvnia, which has lost about 4 percent since the beginning of the year due to the political crisis gripping the country.\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-2-10T12:51:26.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140207ea2700asx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
