\par\par \b \uc2 Ukraine leader seeks cash at Kremlin, Kiev protest planned\b0\par\par\uc2 875 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2013\par 23:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Ukraine's Yanukovich to meet Putin in Kremlin\par \par \uc2 * Loan worth billions of dollars could be agreed\par \par \uc2 * Pro-EU protests planned again for Kiev\par \par \uc2 By Timothy Heritage and Katya Golubkova\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Dec 17 (Reuters) - Ukraine's president could secure loans from Russia on Tuesday when he meets \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  at the Kremlin - money that could help fend off economic crisis as anti-government protests continue in Kiev.\par \par \uc2 Demonstrators demanding that Viktor Yanukovich step down after he spurned a trade and investment deal with the \uc2 European Union\uc2  last month plan a new show of force in Ukraine's capital on Tuesday as the president meets his Russian counterpart.\par \par \uc2 Caught between Western powers, keen to anchor the nation of 46 million in a friendly embrace on the EU's borders, and Moscow, which accuses the West of turning its former Soviet territories against it, Ukraine is in the grip of impending financial crisis that could hit fuel supplies this winter.\par \par \uc2 President Putin, who meets Yanukovich at 3 p.m. (1100 GMT), seems set to agree a loan deal, and possibly offer Ukraine a discount on the Russian natural gas on which its people depend.\par \par \uc2 "The situation in Ukraine is now such that without loans, from one side or another, they will simply fail to maintain economic stability," \uc2 Andrei Belousov\uc2 , an economic adviser to Putin, told Interfax news agency. "I do not rule out that, if there is a request, a credit could be provided."\par \par \uc2 Russia's Finance Ministry\uc2  confirmed talks on a loan were under way. Ukraine's dollar bond prices rallied and debt insurance costs fell as concerns receded that Kiev would become unable to pay its creditors.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's energy minister said a deal was also very probable on lower prices for Russian gas.\par \par \uc2 Despite snow and freezing temperatures, Yanukovich's opponents mustered 200,000 people in Kiev on Sunday to call for his removal and for a free trade pact with the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , which Yanukovich rejected last month after threats from Russia to cut off gas supplies and block Ukrainian imports.\par \par \uc2 They have called for a new demonstration on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Many of those protesting say they fear greater influence from the Kremlin, which exerted oppressive power over Ukrainians during the Soviet period, and see closer ties with the 28-nation EU offering greater freedoms and prosperity.\par \par \uc2 Many are also complaining about Yanukovich's record as he prepares to campaign for re-election in just over a year. Opponents, backed by EU leaders, accuse him of manipulating the judicial system to keep opposition leader Yulia Tymoshenko in jail. Ukrainians also begrudge widespread corruption.\par \par \uc2 EAST VS WEST\par \par \uc2 Agreement on Tuesday would also be seen in Moscow as a triumph for Putin keeping Ukraine in Russia's political and economic orbit more than two decades after the Soviet Union collapsed, and preventing a historic westward shift by Kiev.\par \par \uc2 Underlying the East-West tug-of-war, Sweden's foreign minister, Carl Bildt, accused Moscow on Monday of trying to woo Kiev with propaganda and "sometimes outright lies".\par \par \uc2 His Russian counterpart Sergei Lavrov, meeting EU foreign ministers in Brussels, took a veiled swipe at the bloc by criticising "external \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seeking help to cover an external funding gap of $17 billion next year - almost the level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's depleted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 Putin aide Belousov did not say how much Russia, whose own economy is stuttering badly, would be ready to offer Ukraine. But sources in Ukraine said the deal could be worth $15 billion, with Russian providing about $3-5 billion up front.\par \par \uc2 The most Brussels has so far offered Ukraine is 610 million euros ($838 million) but EU officials are in discussion with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  and other financial institutions on ways to help Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Apart from loans, Ukraine is seeking a lower price for Russian gas - now at around $400 per 1,000 cubic metres - to help it cope with its debt burden.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian Prime Minister \uc2 Mykola Azarov\uc2  says he hopes a deal on cheaper gas prices will soon be concluded. A reduction of at least 10-15 percent is likely, sources in Kiev said.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's talks are intended to conclude a "substantial package" of agreements to chart out a road map to removing trade barriers for Ukraine with Russia, both sides say.\par \par \uc2 Yanukovich is seeking the best deal possible for Ukraine but playing East against West is a hazardous manoeuvre running the risk of alienating both parties and there is no certainty Ukraine can avoid default or a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis.\par \par \uc2 Putin regards Ukraine as vital to creating a political and economic union stretching from the Pacific to the EU's borders. But Yanukovich is not expected to sign Ukraine up for a Russia-led customs union which Putin sees as the basis for this.\par \par \uc2 Holding out on membership of the customs union could be Yanukovich's last bargaining chip as he tries to survive the protests in Kiev and win a presidential election in 2015.\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE/ | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | BNX | G | RBN | RNA | AFA | CSA | LBY | RWSA | RWS | REULB | GNS | ELE | RNP | PGE | PEN | SXNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131216e9cg0014s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
