\par\par \b \uc2 *National Bank Of Ukraine: Reserves Fall To $18.8 Bln In Nov\b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2013\par 15:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 6 Dec 2013 10:29 EDT  Ukraine \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Gold Reserves Fall In Nov Following Unrest\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves of the \uc2 National Bank of Ukraine\uc2  fell $18.79 billion in November on the back of increased demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following widescale protests some of which turned violent, the bank said Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses the reserves to carry out \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , aimed at easing the downside pressure on the hryvnia.\par \par \uc2 The downward pressure increased in late November in particular after Ukrainian President Viktor Yanukovych suddenly refused to sign a trade deal with the \uc2 European Union\uc2 . He had said for some time that he would accept the deal but backtracked and instead blamed Russian trade pressure that was hurting Ukraine's economy.\par \par \uc2 He said Ukraine would seek to improve ties with Russia.\par \par \uc2 In recent days pro-Europe demonstrators took to the streets and some clashed with police trying to disperse the rallies in Kiev.\par \par \uc2 Analysts have warned that negative sentiment towards the hryvnia could intensify after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reports a decline in its reserves, which have nearly halved in the past two years.\par \par \uc2 "That's a pretty big move, down $1.8 billion in the month of November--considering that the unrest only began on Nov. 21, the last third of the month," said Timothy Ash, an analyst at Standard Bank.\par \par \uc2 Reserve depletion is happening faster than expected as the market on average had seen reserves dropping to $19.2 billion, Mr. Ash said.\par \par \uc2 "Excluding gold, reserves likely dropped to around $17 billion, which is now just barely over two months of import cover," he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 06, 2013 10:29 ET (15:29 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131206e9c6001zq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
