\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine central bank \highlight\uc2  ready to do more after  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2013\par 15:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Dec 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vowed on Monday to do what was necessary to uphold financial stability after huge protests against President Viktor Yanukovich at the weekend forced it to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, \uc2 National Bank of Ukraine\uc2  chairman Ihor Sorkin said the bank was ready to increase its presence on "all market segments" to ensure they remained in balance.\par \par \uc2 He added that the bank had not imposed any restrictions on the money and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. He urged depositors to "be confident in the banking system" and not to withdraw their savings.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to sell dollars at 8.1502 hryvnia per dollar, it said on its Reuters terminal page. The bank offered dollars at 8.1397 hryvnia in its previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Nov.14.\par \par \uc2 The government of Mykola Azarov has resisted pressure from the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  to unhitch the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a tight band around 8 hryvnia to the dollar and allow greater flexibility to reduce imports and help narrow the current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 But the government's ability to meet a heavy foreign debt repayment schedule in 2014 is undermined by depleted foreign reserve stocks which at the end of October stood at $20.6 billion - which covers less than two and half months of imports.\par \par \uc2 In his statement, Sorkin expressed confidence that Ukrainian banks could operate well despite the political unrest in the country which followed Yanukovich's U-turn on trade policy away from Europe back towards Russia.\par \par \uc2 "I urge everyone to be confident in the banking system and maintain deposits. Nobody in Ukrainian society has any interest in the destabilisation of the economic situation," he said.\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK/STATEMENT (URGENT,UPDATE 1) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | G | RBN | BNX | RNP | PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131202e9c2000rb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
