\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  cbank did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  much in Feb\b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Februar 2012\par 14:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Cbank says hryvnia no longer under pressure\par \par \uc2 * Dollar peg to remain in place until Oct - analysts\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Feb 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it barely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in February with dollar sales only an eighth of January levels as the hryvnia was well supported by foreign investments and export revenues.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily on the market in late 2011 to support the hryvnia which is pegged at around 8 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The bank did not provide any figures for February but in January, its net foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales stood at $893.6 million.\par \par \uc2 "We barely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market in February," Valery Lytvytsky, the senior adviser to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, told reporters.\par \par \uc2 The bank has spent about $7 billion, nearly a fifth of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, since last September to maintain the peg. The bank's reserves stood at $31.4 billion at the end of January.\par \par \uc2 Lytvytsky said that in February the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  mostly sold foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to state energy firm Naftogaz which makes monthly payments of about $1 billion for imported Russian gas.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine recorded a current account surplus of $395 million in January, although its capital account showed a $1.3 billion deficit.\par \par \uc2 But Lytvytsky said the capital account weakness was temporary and reflected repayments of trade financing loans.\par \par \uc2 "The balance of payments is in a healthy state," he said. "We do not see any threats to hryvnia stability."\par \par \uc2 Ukraine is expected to release its February balance of payments data in early March.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say that the hryvnia peg is likely to remain in place at least until the October parliamentary election because a devaluation would hurt the already sagging ratings of President Viktor Yanukovich's Party of the Regions.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine should be able to maintain exchange rate stability and meet its external financing needs until that time, Renaissance Capital said in a note on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "According to our estimates, the current account gap will be around $7-8 billion to October 2012 which, together with the government's external debt redemptions falling due in this period, results in around $10bn of total external funding Ukraine will need before the elections," it said.\par \par \uc2 "Foreign reserves at $31 billion look sufficient to us to cover both the current account gap and the external debt redemption scheduled for October. Moreover, we note that in January and February we saw an additional supply of dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market which helped reduce pressure on reserves."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Natalya Zinets and Olzhas Auyezov; editing by Anna Willard)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK/HRYVNIA | ABN | M | D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120229e82t000vs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
