\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  cbank says hryvnia to remain stable\b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2012\par 08:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Cbank makes verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support hryvnia\par \par \uc2 * Sold $894 mln last month to maintain dollar peg\par \par \uc2 * Analysts say policy linked to upcoming elections\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Feb 17 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday the hryvnia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been pegged to the dollar since early 2010, would remain stable as the bank took measures to keep its external balance neutral or in surplus this year.\par \par \uc2 "We do not see any reasons for deep devaluation or revaluation (of the hryvnia)," chairman Serhiy Arbuzov said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is taking the necessary measures this year to maintain a normal - positive or neutral - balance of payments and we can say with certainty that the exchange rate will also be in line with forecasts."\par \par \uc2 He did not provide any figures. The hryvnia has so far been pegged at around 8 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The policy became costly last year as a fall in Ukrainian exports, dominated by steel, prompted the trade deficit to more than double to $6.7 billion while the balance of payments gap reached $2.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent about $7 billion, nearly a fifth of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, since last September to maintain the peg.\par \par \uc2 In January alone, the bank's net foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales reached $894 million. The bank's reserves stood at $31.4 billion at the end of January.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say that the hryvnia peg is likely to remain in place at least until the October parliamentary election because a devaluation would hurt the already sagging ratings of President Viktor Yanukovich's Party of the Regions.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Olzhas Auyezov)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK/HRYVNIA  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120217e82h000en\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
