\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  reserves fall after  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2011\par 10:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Cbank burns reserves to protect hryvnia peg\par \par \uc2 * Can go on for a few more months - analyst\par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comments)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Dec 7 (Reuters) - Ukraine's gross foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $32.408 billion as of Nov. 30 from $34.163 billion on Oct. 31, declining for the third month in a row, the state statistics service said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly on the market since September to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg at around 8.0 hryvnias per dollar as foreign investors dumped hryvnia assets and banks and households built up dollar holdings.\par \par \uc2 "The fall in reserves reflects, first, the revaluation of reserves due to the changing euro/dollar rate and, secondly, demonstrates continuing strong demand for cash foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and persisting imbalances in Ukraine's external position where capital inflows do not cover the trade deficit," said Dmitry Fedotkin, an analyst at VTB Capital.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's economy is dominated by steel exports and weakening demand from abroad has already prompted some steel makers to cut output.\par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a separate statement on Wednesday that average daily foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply on the interbank market increased by 12.2 percent month-on-month in November while demand halved.\par \par \uc2 The bank has pledged to maintain the peg until the end of this year and analysts say it may adjust it in 2012. Six-month non-deliverable forwards put the exchange rate at 8.75/9.05 hryvnias per dollar on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "Reserves of $32.4 billion are still enough to maintain exchange rate stability for a few months but if November's dynamics persist in the winter months, the situation on the interbank market will be very complicated," said \uc2 Concorde Capital\uc2  analyst Svetlana Rekrut.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Natalya Zinets and Olzhas Auyezov; editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-RESERVES/  (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111207e7c7000dp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
