\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c.bank says ready to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  all week\b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2011\par 11:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  cbank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  every day since start of year\par \par \uc2 * Significant demand for dollars -- dealers\par \par \uc2 (Adds background)\par \par \uc2 By Natalya Zinets\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday kept up its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since the start of the New Year and said it remained ready to sell dollars at 7.965 hryvnias until the end of this week.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, a bank official told Reuters it would also buy dollars at 7.955 hryvnias <UAH=> per dollar if necessary.\par \par \uc2 "Rates will be maintained at this level until the end of the week and the National Bank will go on to the market as required," press service chief Serhiy Kruglyk said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said they want to buy dollars from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of the significant demand for dollars over the past three days which has pushed the hryvnia down from 7.97 per dollar at the beginning of the week to 7.98 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "There are no offers to sell dollars at the moment. It seems that most people are simply hanging on to dollars, given fluctuations on the market," said a dealer from one large bank.\par \par \uc2 "Usually, at the beginning of the year we have fluctuations towards a weakening of the hryvnia. The imbalance between demand and supply comes from the fact that exporters have not yet woken up after the holidays but we have still to pay for imports," said another \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader.\par \par \uc2 Many dealers say the main reason for the imbalance is the trade deficit -- which stood at $6.9 billion in the first 10 months of 2010 -- and a weak stream of foreign investment.\par \par \uc2 This meant that the market could not handle a high import-driven demand for dollars without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly on the market since September 2010 to offset a high demand for the dollar, selling in all $2.2 billion from September until the end of the year, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures. (Writing by Richard Balmforth; editing by Stephen Nisbet)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-HRYVNIA (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110112e71c000m6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
