\par\par \b \uc2 Ukraine  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  reshuffle may hamper hryvnia\b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2010\par 13:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yanukovich nominates ally to head \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Candidate lacks policy experience, views unclear\par \par \uc2 * Analysts see downside risk for hryvnia <UAH=>\par \par \uc2 By Olzhas Auyezov\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Dec 22 (Reuters) - Ukrainian President Viktor Yanukovich has defied IMF calls for greater \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence by proposing a close associate whose policy views are unknown to head the \uc2 National Bank of Ukraine\uc2  (NBU).\par \par \uc2 Yanukovich nominated Serhiy Arbuzov, 34, to succeed veteran NBU chief Volodymyr Stelmakh on Tuesday, prompting concerns that the hryvnia <UAH=> may weaken further. [ID:nLDE6BK1YK]\par \par \uc2 Parliament, dominated by Yanukovich supporters, is certain to confirm Arbuzov in the job.\par \par \uc2 "Arbuzov's appointment could further streamline the policy making processes in Ukraine although it is likely to have a negative effect on the independence of the NBU, while the IMF is advocating quite the opposite," VTB Capital said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Arbuzov's mother runs a small bank owned by Yanukovich's son Oleksandr and local media say Arbuzov and Oleksandr Yanukovich are close friends.\par \par \uc2 This has led some analysts to believe Arbuzov would be influenced by Ukraine's powerful "steel lobby", which bankrolled Yanukovich's presidential campaign and favours a weaker hryvnia to boost its exports.\par \par \uc2 Before becoming first deputy chairman at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September, Arbuzov ran a small private bank and served for three months as chairman of state Eximbank.\par \par \uc2 MARGINALLY NEGATIVE FOR HRYVNIA\par \par \uc2 "Arbuzov joined the NBU less than four months ago, so we know little about his views on monetary policy," commented Anna Zadornova, an economist at \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "But given his perceived connection to the industrial exporters from the south of the country and lack of experience, we think that the news is on the margin negative for the hryvnia."\par \par \uc2 The hryvnia has been under downward pressure since September as rising imports have pushed up \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account deficit. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to brake the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline.\par \par \uc2 The NBU has ample reserves of $33.5 billion to continue doing so, but outgoing head Stelmakh said this month the bank would be "vigilant" over attempts by trading partners to gain a competitive advantage by devaluing their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund, whose board was due to decide on a $1.6 billion loan tranche later on Wednesday, has repeatedly urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow greater exchange rate flexibility after agreeing a $15 billion stand-by programme in July.\par \par \uc2 One-year non-deliverable forward contracts value the hryvnia at 8.44/8.54 per dollar, down from the current rate of 7.97.\par \par \uc2 "There is an obvious risk that (Arbuzov's) personal stance will be closer to the weak hryvnia policy since he represents the ruling Regions Party," said Oleksandr Valchishen, an analyst at Investment Capital Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Others say, however, that the widely expected reshuffle has already been priced in by the market.\par \par \uc2 "There should be no significant market movements due to these changes," said ING analyst Alexander Pecheritsyn.\par \par \uc2 The hryvnia traded at 7.9690 per dollar on Wednesday, virtually unchanged from Tuesday's close of 7.9700. Ukraine bond spreads were 3 basis points tighter as measured in the \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  emerging market bond index which itself tightened by 2 bp. (Writing by Olzhas Auyezov; Additional reporting by Natalya Zinets; editing by Douglas Busvine/Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK/|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|G|RBN|RNP|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101222e6cm000nh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
