\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine president proposes Arbuzov as cenbank head\b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2010\par 20:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Arbuzov seen as close ally of Yanukovich\par \par \uc2 * Oversaw \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy since Sept (Adds details, background)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Dec 21 (Reuters) - Ukraine's President Viktor Yanukovich proposed on Tuesday appointing Serhiy Arbuzov as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's chairman to replace Volodymyr Stelmakh, the president's press service said.\par \par \uc2 Stelmakh, 71, who has headed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the last six years, has submitted his resignation. Arbuzov, a 34-year-old banker, was appointed Stelmakh's deputy in September. He oversaw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Arbuzov's candidacy has to be approved by the parliament. Yanukovich proposal comes ahead of the International Monetary Fund's vote on Dec. 22 on whether to disburse a $1.6 billion loan tranche to \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the weakening hryvnia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> for the last three months and on Tuesday canceled an old \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulation to clear the way for a law that would make it easier to introduce controls.\par \par \uc2 Arbuzov is seen as an ally of Yanukovich. His appointment in September prompted a hryvnia selloff amid worries that he may be favoring a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support powerful exporters linked to the president.\par \par \uc2 Yanukovich has been strengthening his grip on power after winning presidential elections in January, naming a close ally as prime minister and sidelining the opposition.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's cash-strapped government agreed a $15 billion program with the International Monetary Fund in July, which requires the former Soviet bloc nation to implement unpopular austerity measures and allow greater hryvnia flexibility.\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|UKI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101221e6cl0013f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
