\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-IMF wants more Ukrainian hryvnia flexibility - Ifx\b0\par\par\uc2 171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2010\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Nov 10 (Reuters) - Ukraine's key lender, the International Monetary Fund (IMF), wants greater exchange rate flexibility of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a senior central banker told local media on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The IMF wants us to allow more volatility in the exchange rate movements and follow the market," Interfax news agency quoted first deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Serhiy Arbuzov as saying.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  <USDUAHINV=> regularly this year both when the hryvnia was strengthening against the dollar between February and August and when it started to weaken in September.\par \par \uc2 It has said the hryvnia would not weaken beyond 8.0 per dollar by the end of this year from the current 7.95 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 An IMF mission is in Ukraine until Nov. 15 to review progress and discuss further policies under the $15 billion program agreed in July. (Writing by Olzhas Auyezov)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-IMF/HRYVNIA (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101110e6ba00138\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
