\par\par \b \uc2 Ukrainian hryvnia slips further towards 7.96 per dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2010\par 12:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Nov 2 (Reuters) - The Ukrainian hryvnia <UAH=> slipped further towards the 7.96 to the dollar mark on Tuesday, touching 7.9580 per dollar, due in part to dollar buying by state energy firm Naftogaz, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday traded at 7.9550/7.9570 per dollar, but at the start of dealing on Tuesday bids were at 7.9580/7.96 per dollar, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The hryvnia has been weakening against the dollar since early September as Ukraine's current account deficit widened. The decline has been relatively small, however, compared with gains made earlier this year and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still higher than at the start of the year when it was trading around 8.0 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "We are working at a level of 7.9580/7.96 hryvnia per dollar. This is not cheap but there is no other offer on the market or from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer at one of the biggest banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice last week, selling dollars at 7.9480 per dollar, but has not been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said a major factor pushing down the hryvnia was Naftogaz, which typically buys dollars in the first week of each month to make monthly payments. A Naftogaz representative said last week that the company needed $1 billion to pay for October's gas bill from Russia by Nov 7. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets; Writing by Richard Balmforth; Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-HRYVNIA|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   