\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukrainian hryvnia hits new 6-mth low vs dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2010\par 16:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * C.bank sells $100 mln to support hryvnia\par \par \uc2 * Hryvnia under pressure from cash market - analyst\par \par \uc2 * C.bank comfortable with slow depreciation (Adds c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 19 (Reuters) - The Ukrainian hryvnia <UAH=> extended losses on Tuesday, hitting a fresh six-month low against the dollar and prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling about $100 million on the market.\par \par \uc2 The hryvnia hit 7.953 against the dollar at 1120 GMT, its lowest level since early April and compared with 7.950 at the previous day's close.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  then offered to sell dollars at 7.9440 <NBU01> and sold "about $100 million", a source at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been weakening since early September after the country's current account deficit surged to $563 million, its highest this year, and after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  First Deputy Chairman Anatoly Shapovalov, who was closely involved in exchange rate policy, resigned on Sept. 1 and was replaced by Serhiy Arbuzov, seen as a close ally of President Viktor Yanukovich.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts say the hryvnia's decline -- still relatively small compared with gains made since presidential elections in January -- goes against fundamentals as the country's balance of payments, supported by metals exports, remains healthy.\par \par \uc2 U.S. economist Nouriel Roubini told a conference in Kiev on Tuesday that, overall, the hryvnia "remains slightly undervalued", adding that "appreciation could actually help with reducing inflation" which more than doubled to 2.9 pct in September.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gradual depreciation is being driven by speculative buying of dollars.\par \par \uc2 "The hryvnia remains under pressure from the cash market, as companies and households have been showing interest in buying dollars since August," said a dealer at a Western bank in Kiev.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not in a rush to slow down the process, assuming that a weaker hryvnia will have a positive effect on the economy."\par \par \uc2 A number of emerging market economies are managing exchange rates to avoid fast appreciation against the weakening dollar and maintain economic competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 The dealer also said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  avoided heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as that would prompt dollar holders to postpone converting the greenback into the hryvnia as they expected a more favourable exchange rate in the future.\par \par \uc2 Another local dealer said foreign investors could be selling Ukrainian treasury bills to take profits.\par \par \uc2 "The yields of T-bills are about to bottom out," he said.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's T-bills maturing on Nov. 23, 2011 <UA62012=PFT> yielded 9.05 percent on Tuesday as their price rose 0.15 percent from the previous day's close on the PFTS exchange.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said this week the net influx of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the country had exceeded $5 billion so far this year. But it said the flow of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained volatile as it was dominated by export revenues and loans. (Writing by Andrei Ostrough and Olzhas Auyezov; Additional reporting by Natalya Zinets; Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-HRYVNIA/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101019e6aj0013y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
