\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c.bank supports weakening hryvnia\b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2010\par 13:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Demand for hryvnia falls as VAT bond buy orders fill up\par \par \uc2  * C.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 7.9350 per dollar\par \par \uc2  * More volatility seen ahead\par \par \uc2    (Adds quotes, details, background)\par \par \uc2  KIEV, Sept 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday to support the weakening hryvnia <UAH=> as foreign investor buying of local bonds, which had underpinned the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dried up, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to sell dollars at 7.9350 hryvnias <NBU01> per dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to 7.9400 per dollar, according to Reuters data, matching a multi-month low touched earlier in September after a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reshuffle.\par \par \uc2  "Everybody is buying (dollars)," said a dealer at a foreign bank in Kiev. "Many banks are buying enormous volumes (of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 )."\par \par \uc2  She said the hryvnia had been previously supported by foreign investors who were buying so-called VAT bonds -- special government bonds issued to exporters to settle value-added tax reimbursement arrears. [ID:nLDE67U1YY]\par \par \uc2  But as most of the bonds had now changed hands, foreigners' demand for the hryvnia had fallen.\par \par \uc2  "Looking forward, I see (the dollar) only going up," the dealer said.\par \par \uc2  The hryvnia started weakening against the dollar in early September after a reshuffle at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted concerns of a policy shift. [ID:nLDE68519F]\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since said it saw the hryvnia staying roughly stable until the end of this year and the exchange rate would not fall below 8.0 hryvnias per dollar.\par \par \uc2  But analysts expect more volatility ahead due to Ukraine's pledge to allow more exchange rate flexibility under a deal with the International Monetary Fund and due to political factors such as mayoral and local council elections on Oct. 31.   (Writing by Olzhas Auyezov; Editing by Susan Fenton)  \par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK/HRYVNIA  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100921e69l000p8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
