\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c.bank raises hryvnia  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  rate\b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2010\par 10:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Hryvnia market "balanced" after earlier volatility\par \par \uc2 (Adds dealer comment, background)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Sept 13 (Reuters) - The Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to sell dollars at levels just below market rates on Monday, supporting a stabilisation of its hryvnia <UAH=> \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after losses in the early part of last week.\par \par \uc2 The hryvnia traded at 7.9100-7.9140 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement on Monday, virtually unchanged from levels on last Friday, when it gained a foothold after a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and falls last week.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still down compared to levels seen in late August, when players began to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to worries about a possible change of the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy stance.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the bank offered to sell dollars at 7.9182 hryvnias per dollar <NBU01>, down from 7.9190 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 It also offered to buy dollars at 7.9082 hryvnias <UAH=> per dollar on Monday, it said on its dedicated Reuters page.\par \par \uc2 "The market seems to be balanced," said a trader at one of the local banks. (Writing by Olzhas Auyezov; Editing by Richard Balmforth)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK/HRYVNIA (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100913e69d000jc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley1