\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  hryvnia firms, c.bank discloses  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2010\par 13:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  hryvnia firms to 5-day high vs dollar of 7.908\par \par \uc2 * C.bank ready to buy dlrs at 7.9082 hryvnia, sell at 7.9190\par \par \uc2 * Dealers say move aimed at curbing volatility\par \par \uc2 (Adds details)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Sept 10 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday offered to buy and sell dollars in a move that dealers say was aimed at hampering recently increased volatility in a recovering hryvnia.\par \par \uc2 The Ukranian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its Reuters page <NBU01> said it was ready to buy dollars at the previous day's rate of 7.9082 hryvnia per dollar and sell them at 7.9190 compared to the Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  quote of of 7.9200 <UAH=>.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  defined the frames of the hryvnia rate for today which are close to real market prices. This should bring the volatility down," said a dealer at a Western bank in Kiev.\par \par \uc2 Before recovering to a five-day peak of 7.9080 per dollar on Friday, the hryvnia slid rapidly earlier this month to its weakest since the start of April of 7.94 per dollar from levels of 7.88-7.90 since for the most trading days in August.\par \par \uc2 Market players linked the hryvnia's weakness to increased demand for dollars as Ukrainian gas importer Naftogaz was preparing to settle the payment for Russia's gas worth of $711 million due by September 7. [ID:nLDE6861O7]\par \par \uc2 Currently, the Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market looks balanced, dealers say, and even if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prompted to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it would rather sell dollars at prices above the market.\par \par \uc2 "Today, it was cheaper to buy dollars on the market than at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . What's the point of buying dollars at 7.9190 from the regulator if it's offered ... at lower prices on the market?" said one market player. (Reporting by Natalia Zinets in Kiev and Andrey Ostroukh in Moscow; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-HRYVNIA/(UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100910e69a000mz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
