\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Bulgaria, Hungary CDS rise on debt worries\b0\par\par\uc2 651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2010\par 12:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Bulgaria, Hungary CDS rise on debt worries\par \par \uc2 * Global emerging stocks, debt spreads improve slightly\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine increases \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility as IMF arrives in Kiev\par \par \uc2 * Dubai holds investor roadshow, bond seen unlikely\par \par \uc2 By Carolyn Cohn\par \par \uc2 LONDON, June 10 (Reuters) - The cost of insuring Bulgarian and Hungarian debt against default rose again on Thursday as the debt and deficit position of emerging European economies remained in focus.\par \par \uc2 Hungarian assets slumped last week on comments that Hungary might suffer a Greek-style debt crisis, while the European Commission has queried changes in Bulgarian deficit statistics.\par \par \uc2 Concern about Hungary sent global markets briefly into panic, given existing worries about the debt of peripheral euro zone countries like Greece.\par \par \uc2 "The correction in risky assets will last a bit longer due to technical reasons as well as fundamental concerns about possible contagion of problems in the euro zone area," said James Lord, emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Bulgaria is yet another example of the prevailing market concerns over fiscal sustainability. The question marks over the reliability of Bulgaria's fiscal accounts are obviously not good news and are part of the wider trend across Europe, whether developed or emerging."\par \par \uc2 A surge in Chinese exports provided support for global emerging markets on Thursday, however, although trading ranges were generally subdued ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rate announcement at 1145 GMT, expected to result in steady rates of 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Benchmark emerging equities <.MSCIEF> rose 0.3 percent and emerging sovereign debt spreads <11EMJ> tightened by 3 basis point to 335 bps over U.S. Treasuries.\par \par \uc2 Non-resident bids above 50 percent for a Spanish three-year bond auction also provided some relief. [ID:nLDE6590T9]\par \par \uc2 Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mostly rose, led by a near-1 percent rise in the rand <ZAR=>, with \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows to South Africa helped by the World Cup which kicks off on Friday.\par \par \uc2 DEFICIT FOCUS\par \par \uc2 Hungary's five-year credit default swaps rose 11 basis points to 351 bps, although the forint steadied against the euro <EURHUF=> and stocks climbed 0.5 percent <.BUX>, as investors mulled the government's deficit-cutting plan released this week.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian government's commitment to its 2010 budget deficit goal is "moderately encouraging" but details are lacking and medium-term deficit aims must be clarified, ratings agency Fitch said on Wednesday. [ID:nLDE6581OT]\par \par \uc2 Focus has moved onto Bulgaria, after the European Commission this week demanded Bulgaria explain why it abruptly raised its 2010 budget deficit forecast. [ID:nLDE65827G]\par \par \uc2 Bulgaria's five-year credit default swaps rose 10 basis points to 373.4 bps, according to CDS monitor CMA DataVision, close to 11-month highs hit this week.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's five-year CDS rose to 660.5 bps from 656.1, as a mission from the IMF arrived in Kiev this week.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President Viktor Yanukovich on Wednesday assured the IMF that his country was on track to meet its budget deficit targets as it seeks a fresh $19 billion loan. [ID:nLDE65820X]\par \par \uc2 The IMF also wants more exchange rate flexibility, and \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday adjusted its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate for the third consecutive day, after keeping the rate unchanged for almost two months.\par \par \uc2 Emerging debt issuance has dried up due to ballooning spreads in the past few weeks, but Dubai is meeting investors this week.\par \par \uc2 Dubai has been shut out of international capital markets since state-owned \uc2 Dubai World\uc2  declared a standstill on debt payments in November.\par \par \uc2 "With current risk aversion towards debt markets and further debt restructurings among local quasi-sovereign entities, we see the possibility of a new debt issue rather limited in the short term," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  emerging credit analyst Nuria Jorba said in a client note.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Sujata Rao; Editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100613e66a00065\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
